# Normalize all text to LF in the repo and on checkout, on every platform.
# The site deploys on Linux and the schemas are signed byte-for-byte, so line
# endings must not depend on who committed. This also silences the Windows
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Signatures are computed over exact bytes — never let these be munged.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary

# The ADR-014 interop vectors are normative test data compared byte-for-byte and pinned by committed
# SHA-256 digests (interop/vectors/VECTORS.sha256). The rules above already check them out as LF, but
# they do it by normalising — which is a transformation that a future .gitattributes edit, a stray
# core.autocrlf, or a `git config` on one contributor's machine could change. `-text` disables
# conversion outright, so these files are the same bytes everywhere by construction rather than by
# configuration. Listed after the rules above because the last matching pattern wins.
interop/vectors/**        -text
interop/vectors/*.txt     -text
